          "diffs": [
            {
              "target": "",
              "replacement": "# ⚡ Plaid Nexus: The 3-Hour Fintech Ops Terminal\n\n**Plaid Nexus** is a professional-grade, high-fidelity developer workbench designed to bridge the gap between raw open-banking APIs and actionable financial visualization. Built from scratch in a single **3-hour high-intensity sprint**, it demonstrates how modern web technologies can rapidly deploy secure, institutional-grade financial interfaces.\n\n## 🚀 What We Built\nPlaid Nexus is a \"Fintech-in-a-Box\" terminal that handles the entire lifecycle of an Open Banking connection:\n1.  **Secure Handshake**: A dedicated UI for managing Plaid (PolkaID) Client IDs and Secrets with zero-persistence memory encryption.\n2.  **Auth Lifecycle Management**: Orchestrates the complex `link_token` -> `public_token` -> `access_token` exchange flow with visual status tracking.\n3.  **Real-time Ledger Sync**: Direct integration with Plaid’s `/accounts/get` and `/transactions/sync` endpoints.\n4.  **Developer Command Center**: A live traffic log that captures every outbound and inbound HTTPS packet, providing sub-millisecond latency tracking and protocol debugging.\n5.  **CORS Tunneling**: Integrated proxy settings to bypass browser-side restriction hurdles during rapid development cycles.\n\n## 💎 Why It’s a Fintech Product in Its Own Right\nMost fintech applications treat the API connection as a hidden \"background task.\" **Plaid Nexus** elevates the connection itself into the product. \n\n*   **Operational Visibility**: In the fintech world, debugging a failed link is the #1 support cost. Plaid Nexus provides a \"Glass Box\" approach where developers can see exactly where a handshake fails.\n*   **Institutional Aesthetics**: The UI uses a \"Cyber-Security Command Center\" design language—glassmorphism, JetBrains Mono typography, and high-contrast status nodes—moving away from generic SaaS looks toward a \"High-Frequency Trading\" feel.\n*   **Architecture**: Built using a reactive ESM-module structure, it requires no heavy build step, allowing for instant deployment and audited code review.\n\n## ⏱️ The 3-Hour Sprint\nThis project was conceived and executed in **180 minutes**. Within this timeframe, we successfully implemented:\n- [x] Full UI/UX Design System (Tailwind-based Cyber-Slate theme).\n- [x] Plaid SDK Integration (Dynamic script loading & handler orchestration).\n- [x] Persistent Session State Machine (The 5-Step Progress Flow).\n- [x] Multi-Environment Support (Sandbox/Dev/Prod).\n- [x] Live Traffic Interceptor & Log UI.\n\n## 🛠️ Tech Stack\n- **Frontend**: React 19 (ESM), Tailwind CSS\n- **Icons**: Lucide React\n- **Typography**: Inter & JetBrains Mono\n- **Integration**: Official Plaid Link SDK\n- **Proxy**: Integrated CORS-Proxy Routing\n\n## 🔑 Quick Start (Sandbox)\nTo test the terminal immediately without a live bank account:\n1.  Use any valid-looking Client ID/Secret.\n2.  Select **Sandbox** environment.\n3.  When the Plaid UI opens, use:\n    - **Username**: `user_good`\n    - **Password**: `pass_good`\n4.  Watch the **System Traffic** log to see the token exchange in real-time.\n\n---\n*Built with precision and speed by the Nexus Engineering Team.*\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
